content:
E34 is decisive: messages created t=580–619 are all "done" (445 of them — worker processed these fine after rollback). But messages created t=619–670 are all "pending" with 0 attempts (E31). The worker stopped consuming at ~t=619. E33 shows only 1 open DB session for worker — very low, suggesting the worker has lost its queue connection or is otherwise stuck since t=619. E5 shows messages_processed still rising, which is contradicted by E34 — E5 may be stale/cached metrics. E11/E12 confirm restarts stopped at t=580. This is a runtime fault: the worker process went into a bad state around t=619 after successfully processing the post-rollback backlog.

The orphaned orders (E32: 509 "created" with no live message) are a separate residual damage from the original bad deploy window.

